course: dictionary
lesson: 11214
title: Wonky and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Wonky» is an informal word. To work it out, read the clues around it. «The first Christmas without Da, Cian's family hangs Da's favourite bauble, a wonky robin, right at the front of the tree.» A bauble is a small decoration, and a robin shape that hangs at an angle is not straight.
explain: The clue is "hangs" and "right at the front of the tree". The family is hanging a decoration, so wonky describes how it looks. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a crooked robin" still makes sense, so crooked is right.
explain: Wonky has a second meaning too. A wonky table or wonky Wi-Fi is shaky, weak or not working properly. Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning. A wonky line in art is not straight, so you would use a ruler.
fact: Wonky is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk more than in formal writing.
fact: «Wonky» means crooked, not straight or not level.
fact: «Wonky» can also mean shaky, weak or not working properly, as in «a wonky table».
fact: The forms are wonky, wonkier and wonkiest: «the wonkiest tree» is the most crooked one.
fact: Odd-shaped vegetables sold cheaply to cut waste are called wonky vegetables.
exercise: What does wonky mean in «a wonky robin»? | Covered in snow | Heavy and made of wood | *Crooked, not straight | Shiny and new
exercise: Which meaning of wonky fits «a wonky table» that wobbles when you put a book on it? | *Shaky and weak | Tasty | Very loud | Bright red
exercise: The most crooked tree is the ___ tree. | straightest | wonky | *wonkiest | softest
test: «The shelf is wonky, so the books keep sliding off.» What does wonky suggest? | *Not level or not fixed properly, so it may be shaky | Very sunny | Fast and bouncy | Brand new
test: In an art lesson, a wonky line is not straight. What should you use to make it straight? | A sponge | A crayon | *A ruler | A spoon
exam: Which sentence uses wonky to mean shaky or not working properly? | Cian's bauble was small and round | *The old chair is wonky, so sit down carefully | The robin hung wonky on the tree | Da fell off the ladder in 2019
